    "result": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented the one-line summary feature for CI logs. Here's what was done:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n### 1. **Added `renderSummary()` function** (`src/gate/report.ts`)\n   - Formats output as `<VERDICT> <answered>/<total>`\n   - For BLOCK verdict with failures: appends `: ` and check IDs in GATE_CHECKS order\n   - Special case: `BLOCK 0/7: structure` when the gate section is missing\n   - Warnings don't reduce the answered count\n   - Example: `BLOCK 5/7: evaluation, transparency`\n\n### 2. **Added `--summary` flag to `frai-gate check`** (`src/cli.ts`)\n   - Prints only the one-line summary instead of full report\n   - Maintains exit codes: 1 for BLOCK, 0 for PASS/WARN\n   - `--json` takes priority if both flags are given\n   - Updated HELP text to document the flag\n\n### 3. **Added comprehensive test suite** (`src/gate/report.test.ts`)\n   - 7 tests covering all scenarios:\n     - PASS with all checks answered\n     - WARN with warnings only\n     - BLOCK with multiple failed checks\n     - Structure blocking (gate section missing)\n     - Check order preservation\n     - Deduplication of check IDs\n     - Warning findings ignored in count\n\n## Verification\n- \u2705 All 18 tests pass (7 new + 11 existing)\n- \u2705 Build succeeds: `pnpm --filter frai-gate build`\n- \u2705 Manual testing confirms:\n  - `--summary` outputs one-line format\n  - `--json` takes priority over `--summary`\n  - Exit codes are correct (0 for PASS/WARN, 1 for BLOCK)\n  - HELP text displays the flag properly",
